We have tried a bunch of different things for the routes now, but i think i have gotten a better idea. The idea is: We draw the circle around the balls and place discrete
  pickup points, these are the points where from the robot can pick up the balls, with nothing taken in consideration.

  Then based on proximity to the nearest obstacle, we rank all the pickups points and categorize them. Points with more than tank turn radius distance to the nearest point, get
  marked as safe. These can be approached from all directions with no problem.

  Pickup points with a distance to obstacles equal to the robots tube_forward_cm distance, must be approached from exactly that heading, and thus need an intermediate node, so
  we can tank turn into the right heading from a safe distance. and after pickup the ball we must back up to that intermediate node.

  All the points inbetween these two distances, we need to figure out how to solve. We could either allow for certain approach angles to these points, or also give them
  intermediate nodes. Lets overfocus on this for now, since it is the most complex part of the system. We can always add more categories later if we need to.

  The big win of this approach is that we never should do a tank turn, and possibly turn into an obstacle.

